      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Filing a roof insurance claim in Utah requires documenting the storm damage, getting a professional inspection, and meeting the insurance adjuster on-site."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Step 1: Document the Damage Immediately"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Take photos and videos of missing or cracked shingles, dented vents, flashing, and granules in the gutters before touching anything."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Prevent further damage by tarping leaks or broken areas, and save all emergency repair receipts."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Step 2: Get a Professional Roof Inspection"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Hire a local Utah roofer to perform a detailed inspection before filing."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Get a written report with photos to use as an independent baseline when the insurance company evaluates your roof."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Step 3: File the Claim"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Call your insurance carrier or agent as soon as possible with your policy number, the specific date of the storm or loss, and your initial photo evidence."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Review your deductible and policy limits (such as Actual Cash Value vs. Replacement Cost Value) so you know your financial responsibility."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Step 4: Meet the Insurance Adjuster"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Be present when the insurance adjuster inspects your property."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Have your contractor on the roof with the adjuster to point out storm damage and prevent missed items."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Step 5: Review the Scope and Payout"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Compare estimates line-by-line between your insurance scope and your contractor's bid."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Receive your first check (usually the Actual Cash Value minus your deductible) to begin the work."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Step 6: Complete the Repairs and Release Depreciation"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Schedule your roof replacement or repair with your chosen contractor."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Submit the final invoice to your insurance company once construction finishes to release the remaining depreciation funds."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you need specific guidance, you can check general home claim rules via the Utah Insurance Department .",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Utah Insurance Department",
            "link": "https://insurance.utah.gov/consumers/home-insurance/home-claims-info/"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like more tailored guidance, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What type of storm caused the damage (hail, heavy wind, heavy snow)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "When did the damage happen?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you prepare for the next steps."
      },
